# cockpit-wireguard, Windows client .envdefault
#
# Seeded by deploy.ps1 to C:\ProgramData\edt1-wg\.env, MISSING-ONLY. Same grammar
# as the Linux .envdefault and for the same reason: KEY=value, no export, no
# interpolation, full-line comments only. See cockpit-secrets/source/docs/
# DEPLOY-CONTRACT.md section 4.1.
#
# LOCATIONS AND SETTINGS ONLY. The tunnel's PrivateKey is NOT here and must never
# be: it belongs in the .conf that WireGuard imports, which lives in WireGuard's
# own DPAPI-protected configuration store once imported.

# The tunnel name WireGuard uses. The hook script is invoked with
# %WIREGUARD_TUNNEL_NAME% and this is what it should match; it is also the name
# shown in the WireGuard UI. Wrong value: the hooks run against a tunnel that
# does not exist and the PostUp reachability check fails every time.
WG_TUNNEL_NAME=edt1-split

# The local container subnet on THIS machine that should reach edt1 through the
# tunnel. wg-hooks.ps1 adds a route for it on PostUp and removes it on PostDown.
# Leave EMPTY to disable that handling entirely, which is correct on a laptop
# that runs no containers.
WG_CONTAINER_SUBNET=

# Where the hook script's undo journal is written. Under ProgramData because it
# must survive an upgrade - the payload is replaced wholesale and a journal lost
# mid-tunnel leaves routes and the forwarding flag un-restored.
WG_UNDO_JOURNAL_DIR=C:\ProgramData\edt1-wg\state
